issue.description:
Polish the Workbench top toolbar so the recovery actions and persistence/export actions read as two clear visual groups.

Owner direction:

* Add pointer cursor behavior to the new Undo, Redo, and Reset buttons.
* Add a short vertical separator between the recovery actions and the export/save actions.
* Rename "Export JSON" to "Export".

Visual grouping intent:

```
Undo   Redo   Reset   |   Export   Save
```

The separator is visual only. Do not add unnecessary structural wrappers if the current markup can support the divider cleanly.

Separator requirements:

* vertical line/border;
* positioned between Reset and Export;
* approximately the same visual height as the toolbar buttons/icons;
* do not stretch it to the full toolbar height;
* keep alignment centered with the action controls;
* use existing semantic border styling/tokens rather than a hard-coded arbitrary color where possible.

Cursor behavior:

* Undo -> cursor pointer when enabled/interactive.
* Redo -> cursor pointer when enabled/interactive.
* Reset -> cursor pointer when enabled/interactive.
* Preserve disabled-state semantics; disabled actions should not misleadingly present as interactive.

Label change:

* "Export JSON" -> "Export"
* Preserve the existing export action, icon, behavior, and file format. This is label-only.

Preserve:

* existing icon sizes;
* existing toolbar height;
* current action order;
* current spacing/alignment unless a minor adjustment is needed to accommodate the separator;
* existing hover/focus/disabled states;
* Save label/icon/behavior;
* keyboard accessibility and focus order.

Do not:

* change undo/redo/reset behavior;
* change export file format or payload;
* change save behavior;
* introduce unrelated toolbar redesign.

Acceptance:

* Undo, Redo, and Reset show pointer cursor when enabled.
* Disabled recovery actions retain correct disabled cursor/semantics.
* A short vertical separator appears between Reset and Export.
* Separator height is approximately button-height, not full toolbar height.
* "Export JSON" is displayed as "Export".
* Toolbar alignment remains visually balanced.
* No regressions to keyboard navigation, focus states, recovery actions, export, save, or accessibility.
